Notebook[{
Cell["IsomorphicHypergraphQ", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"1a22d825-f421-be43-aa71-f6fb76554d06"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"IsomorphicHypergraphQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"hg1", ",", " ", "hg2"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"13bb1db9-9829-a945-8632-21162dce9547"],
 " ",
 "gives True if hg1 and hg2 are isomorphic as labelled hypergraphs."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"60f28c0e-f6a6-d44f-b922-7e66a98a8df0"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"a5a0bbbf-5376-734b-8c8e-9f3932983f4e"],

Cell["\<\
Some renaming of vertex identifiers must carry hg1 onto hg2: the edge \
multisets must match exactly, each edge matching up to its own symmetry type, \
with edge multiplicities preserved.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"28a13a52-ed5a-f74b-a0ea-6a1c51f7394a"],

Cell["\<\
The renaming must also carry the labels of hg1 onto those of hg2 by a \
one-to-one correspondence. Labels are therefore significant only up to \
renaming: what must agree is which elements share a label, not what the \
labels are called.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4376e3a8-5536-cf4d-a754-0a30a2203463"],

Cell["\<\
Vertex labels and edge labels are put in correspondence independently of one \
another.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b28a245f-6083-344f-88cb-0428c45c237f"],

Cell["\<\
An element with no label can correspond only to an element with no label. \
Without this, every unlabelled hypergraph would be isomorphic to a labelled \
one whose labels were all alike.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ebb125d0-a4c1-3a4c-97df-43f66529cfe2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Labeled\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"26a81e75-5dd1-9649-aabd-1d2e6d0c4303"],
 " the skeletons are compared instead, ignoring labels altogether. Labelled \
isomorphism always implies isomorphism of skeletons."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0dfdb2a5-c020-d248-a2da-b8443216a0c0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Method", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2b93cc05-9bf5-7741-9d7d-5d3ca0616b1c"],
 " option is as for CanonicalHypergraph. Both settings always agree here."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e42d810e-e6c0-6549-8341-60fffec0a427"],

Cell["\<\
The search is exhaustive, and is comfortable up to roughly eight vertices.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"89482051-90d8-4c40-813d-42c1dea5109c"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"c81936a1-b178-414c-ae9a-b83648fc7618"],

Cell["The same directed path on different identifiers:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"2060521b-86f9-2040-a7cb-3e064df52b5b"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}], Hypergraph[{{10, 20}, \
{20, 30}}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}], Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {1, \
3}}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"11824764-b7a6-b647-959f-012db23e0ec7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"True", ",", "False"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"1e47a9e8-\
797d-e547-9a00-5894bddd9b4e"],

Cell["\<\
Symmetry types are respected: a directed path is not an unordered one, but an \
unordered path on three vertices is an unordered star:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"5329c005-65c0-dd4d-becf-1a509a270bd7"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}],
                       Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}],
                       Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{1, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"84fff00c-0c38-ee42-b489-feeed9e630b5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"88f92dd4-\
9ceb-594e-9aae-afe7208a12cb"],

Cell["\<\
Labels count only up to a one-to-one renaming. Here a, b corresponds to x, y:\
\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"f5b23e5e-4732-3145-bf00-24b01d4e65c4"],

Cell["\<\
h1 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"a\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Directed\", \"b\"]}];
h2 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"y\"]}];
IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h2]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a885b38f-77b3-2847-9d75-e6576f58b0f8"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"cafe1882-7191-6947-a33e-80839ab794c2"],

Cell["\<\
But h3 repeats a single label where h1 has two distinct ones, and no \
correspondence can do that:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"dc623b64-2a4e-a649-92a9-13b0d08f477d"],

Cell["\<\
h3 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"x\"]}];
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h3], IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h3, \"Labeled\" -> \
False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"042ffc68-0aa9-2a4a-acc1-882501cb9ee9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"fd679f2c-\
e0cf-564f-b279-a3e6958f9231"],

Cell["\<\
The same principle governs vertex labels. A, A, B against A, B, B is not an \
isomorphism, because A would have to correspond to both A and B:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"26c16086-b97b-774c-a29b-dca34d260168"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"A\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}],
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"C\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}],
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"C\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"A\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"16f244fe-f148-554d-a8c0-df2a99aa7107"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"94fc47ae-\
987a-5a4f-a1c9-31133d14b777"],

Cell["An unlabelled edge is not a labelled one:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"6a6259f3-da42-fe47-a131-150a8d955b4f"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"f\"]}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}]}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"f\"]}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}]}],
                       \"Labeled\" -> False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4bfad549-b78f-2d47-9e03-4ae108d3b21f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"3599d18f-\
061a-f042-8635-462861843cfd"],

Cell["Source", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"66366073-d818-0b4c-86ce-33d4a4ee0133"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Defined in ",
 StyleBox["src/Hypergraph.wl",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Plain"],
 ", section ",
 "\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 "Canonical form and isomorphism",
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b2349100-61d2-ff4c-a204-bed9377b2983"],

Cell["See Also", "SeeAlsoSection",ExpressionUUID->"bbad4795-21ac-9a4e-a6c3-c12ac7c30cba"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["FindHypergraphIsomorphism", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"88e8a3c4-c775-734b-a91f-599570ad15e2"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["CanonicalHypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"01fca772-affe-084c-970a-b83088959200"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphSkeleton", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"24f27ded-23e8-ab44-a0a3-cfab9d8bd24a"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Hypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ceb65035-5aba-204d-86b6-3af5a667ca67"]
}], "SeeAlso",ExpressionUUID->"32b41c7f-7383-1148-b4aa-d0f24ac893fa"]
},
WindowSize->{800, 750},
